        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Anxiety and sleep symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports feeling “on edge all the time” for approximately 3–4 months, worse over the last few weeks, with worry about job and money. Trouble falling asleep with racing thoughts; sleeps approximately 5–6 hours and does not feel rested. Uses phone late at night and thinks it is probably not helping."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Anxiety-associated physical symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports palpitations, chest tightness, a knot in the stomach, and mild nausea when anxious. No shortness of breath. No panic attacks."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and safety symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mood a bit low, but still enjoys time with children and fishing when not too tired. Denies anhedonia and hopelessness. Denies suicidal ideation and self-harm."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Caffeine, alcohol, and other substance use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports two coffees and 2–3 energy drinks daily. Alcohol mainly on weekends, 4–6 standard drinks. Reports no drug use and is a non-smoker."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental state examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Looks well, a bit tense and fidgety. Speech normal; thoughts coherent. Anxious but appropriate, with good insight and judgement. No psychotic features."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Psychiatric and substance-use history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports no past psychiatric diagnosis and no medications. No red flags for psychosis, bipolar disorder, or substance use disorder today."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right scrotal swelling, reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports right scrotal swelling for approximately 6–8 months, slowly getting bigger; painless but feels heavy by the end of the workday. Denies redness, fever, urinary symptoms, weight loss, and night sweats. Patient is worried it might be cancer and reports that it transilluminates with a phone torch."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right hemiscrotum enlarged and non-erythematous. Soft, fluctuant swelling around the testis, non-tender. Right testis palpable with normal consistency and no discrete hard mass felt. Right side transilluminates. No cough impulse, obvious inguinal hernia, or inguinal lymph nodes. No clinical red flags for torsion, strangulated hernia, or testicular tumour."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
